			<div class="content" id="post-content-2530708">
									

<p>I would argue that having a pattern limits the spook factor: because if there's a consistent pattern, it can be extrapolated upon. If it can be extrapolated upon, then you can start making predictions. If you can predict where the boxes appear, even only partially accurately, then you have essentially boxed in the boxes and turned them into anomalous fishbowls. The unpredictability of the spaces is what helps make this so horrifying.</p>

